{"duration_api_ms":2573,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7c3f220e-d127-42ea-b179-d84c51d6fcb4","total_cost_usd":0.000631,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1092,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":474,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":69},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1092,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":474,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1092},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1636,"outputTokens":498,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":1092,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.000631,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":69,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":1092,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Key steps** (verify against the fund's notices, since timing varies):\n\n1. **Read the notices** for the shareholder vote or proxy, conversion date, and record date. Conversions are often structured as tax-free reorganizations.\n2. **Note your cutoffs:** the last day to buy, redeem, or exchange into the mutual fund, and when automatic investment plans stop.\n3. **Confirm where your shares will sit.** Direct-held accounts may convert automatically at the transfer agent or require a move to a brokerage. If you must act, start an ACATS or in-kind transfer early.\n4. **Expect fractional-share handling.** ETFs generally trade whole shares, so fractions are typically cashed out, which can be taxable. Confirm the treatment and whether your broker supports fractional ETF shares.\n5. **Adjust trading habits.** You'll buy and sell on an exchange through a brokerage, using limit orders to manage bid-ask spreads. Redemption at NAV no longer applies.\n6. **Review dividends and taxes.** Reinvestment settings and distribution schedules may change.\n\nA full conversion differs from adding an ETF share class, which typically leaves existing mutual fund holdings unchanged.","ttft_ms":773,"type":"result","duration_ms":2040,"uuid":"fec0288f-7d8c-4613-9812-02c621907c85","ttft_stream_ms":431,"time_to_request_ms":63,"first_content_frame_ms":431,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
